{"actions":[],"cardId":"cardid_64de6c49bb2eb9b42a3e07f8d00ab768","createdAt":"2026-03-13T23:51:00Z","expiresAt":"2026-03-15T23:51:00Z","icon":"square.grid.2x2","id":"card_4bfe9bd5056bba4c74122bf9a633a33c","message":"The article you asked about tonight — moving from single AI tasks to recursive task-class factories — has real-world validation arriving this week.","metadata":{"height":400,"htmlContent":"<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><meta name='color-scheme' content='light dark'><style>:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#ffffff);--text:var(--fw-text,#111827);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#6b7280);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#9ca3af);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(15,23,42,0.08));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#2563eb);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#f3f4f6)}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:var(--fw-bg,#1c1c1e);--text:var(--fw-text,#f2f2f7);--muted:var(--fw-text-secondary,#a0a0a0);--tertiary:var(--fw-text-tertiary,#707070);--border:var(--fw-border,rgba(255,255,255,0.1));--accent:var(--fw-accent,#4b93ff);--surface:var(--fw-surface,#2a2a2a)}}body{margin:0;padding:20px;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text);background:var(--bg)}*{box-sizing:border-box}h4{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 4px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3}.subtitle{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.4}.msg{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.5}.divider{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:0}.item{padding:12px 0}.item-title{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 4px}.item-desc{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.45;margin:0}.item a{color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none}.item a:hover{text-decoration:underline}</style></head><body><h4>Your task-factory article has fresh ammunition</h4><div class='subtitle'>Academic papers and industry posts are converging on exactly what you described</div><p class='msg'>The article you asked about tonight — moving from single AI tasks to recursive task-class factories — has real-world validation arriving this week.</p><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><div class='item-title'><a href='https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.08234' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>SkillRL (arXiv)</a> — agents that evolve via recursive skill augmentation</div><div class='item-desc'>Reinforcement learning agents that build new skills from old ones, then compose those skills into higher-order capabilities. Exactly your “task class factory” framing.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><div class='item-title'><a href='https://www.emergence.ai/blog/towards-autonomous-agents-and-recursive-intelligence' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Emergence AI</a> — recursive intelligence and agent self-assembly</div><div class='item-desc'>Their vision: agents create goals, simulate tasks, evaluate themselves, and generate new specialized agents as code. Multi-agent systems that assemble on demand.</div></div><hr class='divider'><div class='item'><div class='item-title'>Your 11-day progression is the case study</div><div class='item-desc'>Single task → recurring task → self-evaluating task → task class with process improvement → factory of factories. You’ve lived every stage. The article should lead with lived experience, then layer in the academic framing.</div></div></body></html>"},"priority":"medium","state":"active","subType":"suggestions","subtitle":"Academic papers and industry posts are converging on exactly what you described","timestamp":"2026-03-13T23:51:00Z","title":"Your task-factory article has fresh ammunition","type":"html-webview"}
